WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:01.632
- Welcome back.

00:00:01.632 --> 00:00:03.130
We've got Whitney Cummings,
The Property Brothers,

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.813
and Andrea Pitter with us.

00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:05.869
Give it up, y'all.

00:00:05.869 --> 00:00:08.140
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.820
That was a clip from last
time Heidi Klum was here.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.620
She restored me, I'm pretty sure.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.370
We played a game in honor of
her show, "Making the Cut."

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:18.167
We now have the winner
of "Making the Cut" here.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.310
So, it's time for another
round of "Making the Cut,"

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.175
but with--

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:22.008
(button dings)
(Whitney laughs)

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:23.063
- [Drew] Wait. Wait.

00:00:23.063 --> 00:00:26.156
♪ Making the cut, but with what ♪

00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:26.989
- [Drew] Oh, okay. Sorry.

00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:29.410
- [Jonathan] Why don't we
get those long hand things?

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.980
- That's what we had to do in COVID.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.674
We can touch it now.

00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:35.351
- By the way, none of this
episode is going to make the cut.

00:00:35.351 --> 00:00:36.510
But, it's been a blast.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.071
- It's already been cut.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.137
(laughing)

00:00:39.137 --> 00:00:40.840
- Wait, teams are me
and Jonathan, winners,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.480
versus Whitney and Drew, losers.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.870
Andrea has graciously agreed to host.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.681
So, take it away, Andrea.

00:00:47.681 --> 00:00:49.236
(laughing)

00:00:49.236 --> 00:00:50.069
Good luck.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:51.220
- Okay. Fair and square.

00:00:52.097 --> 00:00:53.740
In this quiz, the answer to each question

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.010
is something or someone that cuts.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.510
The first team to hit the buzzer

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.640
and give the right answer gets the point,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.435
and steals are allowed.

00:01:01.435 --> 00:01:02.883
- [Jonathan] Wait, how do you steal?

00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:03.716
- Oh, if they get it wrong.

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:04.549
- If they get it wrong.
- Oh, I see.

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:05.672
- When you get it wrong.

00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:06.706
(laughing)

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:07.539
- Oh my God.

00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:09.276
- I love you! I love you!

00:01:09.276 --> 00:01:10.217
- I am so stressed out.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.730
- If Kelly and Jonathan win,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.932
the right side of the
audience gets a prize.

00:01:14.932 --> 00:01:18.780
(Kelly mimics air horn blaring)

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.550
If Whitney and Drew
win, it's the left side.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.700
And their photos go up

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.610
on the Blake Shelton Wall of Champions

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:26.530
who beat Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.635
- It's a dumb wall. It's a dumb wall.

00:01:28.635 --> 00:01:29.979
- Why does that guy put
his name on everything?

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:31.823
- It's a dumb wall.
- "It's a dumb wall."

00:01:31.823 --> 00:01:33.000
- Let's go. Here's the first question.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.386
Paul Bunyan used one of these.

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:36.219
(button dings)

00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:37.052
- Axe.

00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:38.286
(bell chimes affirmatively)

00:01:38.286 --> 00:01:39.869
(Kelly screams)
- What!

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:41.452
- Oh my Gosh! What!

00:01:42.681 --> 00:01:44.628
- Okay, okay, okay. Okay. You know what?

00:01:44.628 --> 00:01:45.844
- Hold on, she pays the producers.

00:01:45.844 --> 00:01:48.393
- No! I have never seen--
- No, no, no, no.

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:49.924
I am, you know what--
- I have never seen a thing!

00:01:49.924 --> 00:01:51.490
- The way-- how quickly someone answers

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.360
tells you everything you
need to know about the person

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.510
and their own stuff.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.710
Kelly has bunions and
cuts them with an axe,

00:01:58.263 --> 00:01:59.376
so that's why that came so quickly to her.

00:01:59.376 --> 00:02:01.787
- No! You know those little
plays you had to do in school?

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.014
I always remembered him having an axe.

00:02:03.014 --> 00:02:04.154
That's why, that's why.

00:02:04.154 --> 00:02:05.092
- If you didn't buzz, I was gonna buzz.

00:02:05.092 --> 00:02:05.925
- Yeah.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:06.758
- Here's the next one.

00:02:06.758 --> 00:02:08.115
This X-Man has claws--

00:02:08.115 --> 00:02:08.948
(button dings)

00:02:08.948 --> 00:02:09.886
- Yes!
- Yeah!

00:02:09.886 --> 00:02:11.260
- You knew it!

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.550
- Wolverine.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.383
(bell chimes affirmatively)

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.216
Boom.

00:02:14.216 --> 00:02:15.049
- Bring it in!

00:02:15.049 --> 00:02:15.882
- Boom!

00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:16.715
- Are we still close?

00:02:16.715 --> 00:02:18.092
- Yeah, no, you have to get closer.

00:02:18.092 --> 00:02:19.500
- I love that he's like, so tall.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.270
I'm like, doing this to his belly button.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.110
- It's a belly button bounce, right there.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.641
Hold on. Go sideways to the camera.

00:02:25.641 --> 00:02:27.490
- Like, like, it's like,
it's like, this is--

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.426
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:28.426 --> 00:02:30.650
- So the game is hit the button,
whether you have it or not.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.920
- Yeah.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.283
- Let's keep going.

00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:34.540
(Whitney laughing)

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.040
If you pass gas,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.300
you might be said--
(button dings)

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.770
- Come on!
- Gut disease!

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.329
- But there's that--
(bell chimes affirmatively)

00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:42.054
- Yeah!
- What in the world!

00:02:42.054 --> 00:02:42.887
Oh my God!

00:02:42.887 --> 00:02:43.864
- It's not a game anymore.

00:02:43.864 --> 00:02:46.998
It's rigged.
- We are on fire!

00:02:46.998 --> 00:02:49.479
Here's the next one: During surgery--

00:02:49.479 --> 00:02:50.569
(laughing)

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:52.837
- Uh, scalpel, scalpel, scalpel.

00:02:52.837 --> 00:02:53.703
Scalpel.

00:02:53.703 --> 00:02:54.902
- Scalpel.

00:02:54.902 --> 00:02:55.735
(bell chimes affirmatively)

00:02:55.735 --> 00:02:56.568
- Yes!
- See!

00:02:56.568 --> 00:03:00.552
(audience cheering)
(Whitney laughing)

00:03:00.552 --> 00:03:02.624
- That was amazing.

00:03:02.624 --> 00:03:05.093
She said, "During surgery,"
I thought (indistinct)

00:03:05.093 --> 00:03:07.205
- But wait--
- Let's do it again!

00:03:07.205 --> 00:03:08.593
Let's do it, now that I
know we're in the game!

00:03:08.593 --> 00:03:09.990
- This is the best part.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.279
That was actually worth three points.

00:03:12.279 --> 00:03:14.256
(bell chimes affirmatively)
(cheering)

00:03:14.256 --> 00:03:15.727
- Yes!
(Whitney laughing)

00:03:15.727 --> 00:03:19.969
- No! The last question is
always worth three points.

00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:21.926
(Whitney laughs)
- [Drew] We're still in this!

00:03:21.926 --> 00:03:23.259
- So we're tied!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.190
How do we settle this?

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.700
- Uhh.
- Deathmatch?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.100
- All right. Bring us scissors.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.640
- [Kelly] That was amazing.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.900
They cut, too.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.959
- Tiebreaker.
- Tiebreaker.

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:35.210
- Okay, the tiebreaker.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.043
Are we ready?

00:03:36.043 --> 00:03:37.200
- Yes.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.720
- Okay. You can cut up fruit--

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.553
(button dings)

00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:40.421
- Oh.

00:03:40.421 --> 00:03:42.295
- Uh, dicer. Dicer?

00:03:42.295 --> 00:03:43.390
- No.
- No?!

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.793
- We get the whole question.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.500
- You can cut up fruit and veggies

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.200
for your smoothie in one of these.

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:51.000
- (whispering) A Vitamix?

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:51.833
- Like, a blender?

00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:52.666
- Like, a Vitamix?

00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:53.499
- Yeah.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.332
- No, no.

00:03:54.332 --> 00:03:56.076
Microwave. Microwave.
- Do you have to be specific?

00:03:56.076 --> 00:03:57.170
- Do you know those
things that cut apples?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.450
It's like a circle, and you go--

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.185
- Oh! That was exactly the answer.

00:04:02.185 --> 00:04:03.562
(cheering)
(bell chimes affirmatively)

00:04:03.562 --> 00:04:04.395
- Boom!

00:04:04.395 --> 00:04:05.228
- What did you say?

00:04:05.228 --> 00:04:08.930
(audience cheering)

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.509
- Okay, well, hold on, hold on.

00:04:11.509 --> 00:04:12.896
Let's just do one all-or-none.

00:04:12.896 --> 00:04:14.160
One all-or-none.
(air horn blaring)

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.900
One all-or-none.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.780
- Wait, I got this. It's okay.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.257
Our side, I'm going to
renovate all your houses. So--

